From 040afe9256e2de31830fb266361985ab96ba6cbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:01:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NET PLAY: nothing on the panel that cannot act, and say what
 discovery did

START does nothing until somebody has joined, and OPTIONS belongs to the
screen behind this one. Both sat on the top row looking pressable and were
not, and between them they were the reason the text had so little room.
Gone from this panel. EXIT now goes back to the screen NET PLAY was opened
from rather than quitting the game - stepping into a panel and finding its
corner button closes everything would be a nasty surprise.

The two things the host genuinely does need - choosing the mission and
starting it - are rows in the list's own style now, and drawn only when
there is a host to use them. The mission arrows do nothing on this screen
otherwise, where before they quietly changed a value nothing was showing.

With the top row free the text starts at y 34 and the list at 52.

Now the part that matters more. "They cannot see each other" is three
different faults wearing the same face - nothing is being sent, something
is sent but nothing arrives, or something arrives and is not understood -
and they want completely different fixes. Nothing here could tell them
apart: network_send_broadcast's return value was thrown away, and a
datagram that arrived and was not a beacon was indistinguishable from no
datagram at all.

So the send result is kept, beacons sent and heard are counted along with
every datagram that reaches the discovery socket, and the panel says so
under an empty list: "sent 40, heard 0 from 0 packets" is a blocked port,
"heard 0 from 12 packets" is a fault in this file, and "discovery off -
UDP port 6511 refused" is the socket never opening. The same line goes to
settlers_net.log every thirty seconds or so, so a session that did not
work can be read back rather than described.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFktm5o1kLnS2Pgvyp8tD4
